  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe here the feature you are requesting. -->\r\nI had some trouble because my server updates automatically. since version .29 synapse introduced a new configuration requirement on apache2 (x-forward-proto) which lead to some errors which i was not aware of.\r\nwhen in this moment one tried to contact another person on my server (e.g. from @matrix.org to @mysmallhomeserver.com) the key exchange seemed to fail. thats not a big deal because i noticed that error in the logs and followed the migration guide (adding that x proto forward header).\r\nbut it was impossible since then to communicate with the person. he was able to read my messages and he has seen that i have seen his messages, but i was unable to read them. \r\ni had to manually verify him with the emojis - after that it worked. i guess that \"broken\" key (or no key at all) has been exchanged and was not updated automatically.\r\ni am a technical person and was able to fix that but i guess most people have no idea what to do in that case.\r\n\r\nwould it be possible to somehow popup a messagebox \"the key does not match or is not existent, would you like to verify the other person manually?\" and when pressed \"yes\", popup the emojis for manual verification.\r\n\r\nif i should create this in the client instead of synapse, please let me know.",
